    "turn_text": "We all desire to be fully and wholly loved, valued for who we are. Hi, I'm Hans, CEO of the Lighthouse Mission. Spend a day in a homeless person's shoes and you'll understand their depth of fear, pain and helplessness. The feeling of being too far gone to come back, not even knowing what you feel anymore, except alone, scared and hungry. Until one day you come to the mission, meeting people with real passion for your well-being and a competency to see you through, you finally feel safe. You sleep in peace. You discover you're not a mistake. The God loves you, and homelessness doesn't have to define you. This kind of community is the best solution I've ever known. Honestly, housing isn't the problem. That alone won't solve homelessness. It's about connection, and a shift in identity. The Lighthouse Mission is a little garden of Eden, right here in Bellingham, where lives find traction, fueled with purpose, meaning and joy. Are you ready to inspire hope to build a brighter future? Help provide the financial fuel today that will change lives for tomorrow at TheLighthouseMission.org. We can't do it alone.",
